@native-plugin-install
Feature: Plugin management input and native TLS contracts
  Scenario: Plugin management inputs preserve sources identifiers and optional reasons
    Then plugin management inputs preserve native sources correlation and reconciliation reasons
  Scenario: Owner supplied native CA files cannot use untrusted paths links or contents
    Then native CA roots require owned canonical bounded certificate files and retain their content identity
  Scenario: Plugin management models keep portable native results and independent grants
    Then plugin management models preserve native responses portable graphs and isolated owner grants
  Scenario: Plugin management receipts cannot authorize another mutation or runtime
    Then plugin authority receipts bind each method input result and unchanged nonconfiguration ownership
  Scenario: Plugin reconciliation verifies bounded deltas and preserves partial failures
    Then plugin reconciliation retains per pass failures and rejects unrelated cache settings and invalid deltas
  Scenario: Plugin source preparation rejects unsafe provenance with parameter diagnostics
    Then plugin source preparation identifies escaped local files Git options npm registry credentials and mismatched remote IDs
